.TH TR2IMG 1
.SH NAME
tr2img \- a page of troff's output as an image
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B tr2img
[
.BI -p " page"
] [
.BI -r " dpi"
] [
.BI -d " dir"
] [
.I file
]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Tr2img
paints a page of what
.IR troff (1)
wrote (its
.I file
or its standard input) as the document views paint it (Xenith's,
.IR wm/page (1)):
its glyphs from the device's outline fonts, its drawings and its images
.RB ( "x X image" ,
as
.IR tr2pdf (1)
places them), and writes it on its standard output as a PPM image.
.TP
.BI -p " page"
The page, from 1 (1).
.TP
.BI -r " dpi"
Its resolution, in dots to the inch (72).
.TP
.BI -d " dir"
The directory an image's name is from, if it is not rooted (the
current directory).
.SH EXAMPLES
.IP
.EX
troff -mbook book.ms >book.out
tr2img -p 3 -r 150 book.out >page3.ppm
.EE
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/cmd/tr2img.b
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR troff (1),
.IR tr2pdf (1)
